# Owner standing requests (digest, 2026-11-10)
Short list of what Ahmed asked for in chat and still expects. Written so a compaction or a new model never loses it. No private AHome content here. When a line is finished and verified, move it to the bottom under "Verified" with the date and the evidence.

## How HQ works
1. HQ (Claude) is the manager only: it gives orders, reviews and writes briefs. Building is done by Antigravity (Gemini) and the free CLI agents. Screen control is done by a Haiku operator at the lowest effort.
2. Worker order: `ops/ACCOUNT_ROTATION.md`, block CURRENT ORDER. Free Antigravity accounts in both Chrome profiles first, then Kilo, OpenCode, Devin CLI, then ZCode accounts, then Pro accounts after resets, then the paid account, Codex very late, HQ last. Never Claude 4.x.
3. Keep a usage record for every account and tool (`ops/agy-accounts-usage.md`, `ops/ACCOUNT_LEDGER.md`) and come back to each account at its reset.
4. The Haiku operator: presses "Restart to update" in Antigravity, reads usage after each switch, sends "continue" with ctrl+Enter to every chat, presses Retry on errors, skips exhausted accounts by itself.
5. Every worker commits, pushes and checkpoints after each step, so a cut-off loses nothing.
6. Look for other free CLIs or IDEs with strong free models, install them and add them to the rotation.
7. Web research is allowed for agents; never with private data.

## Telegram and personal assistant
8. Bot with tap buttons (status, queue, clean disk, approvals), photos, files and short summaries. Projects and HQ report there.
9. SIR Jobs must send only NEW jobs, never the same file again.
10. Watch WhatsApp, Telegram, class groups and email in the main Chrome profile and summarize what is new (`plans/INBOX_ASSISTANT.md`). Drafts only; one-tap approval before anything is sent as him.
11. SIR Jobs prepares the first application for the best jobs; the auto-submit switch stays OFF until he approves. Goal: first income from AI this month.
12. Remind him of the best time to press the weekly Claude Reset (task exists: Wed 2026-11-11 13:00, never later than 2026-11-16).

## Laptop
13. Services started by Antigravity must run at logon and survive closing Antigravity or Claude: listener, smart alert, reminder counter.
14. At boot open Claude, Antigravity, Chrome and the other tools. When a game from `D:\Games` starts, close them and lighten the system; reopen them after the game.
15. No flashing CMD windows anywhere (Laptop Manager, its site, scheduled tasks, Telegram scripts).
16. Laptop Manager: safe disk cleanup (caches, empty folders), update all programs and CLIs with retry on errors.

## Every product
17. Support AI assistant, modern AI features, self-running operation.
18. SEO and AI-answer visibility ahead of competitors; competitor research (features, flaws, complaints).
19. Legal pages per country so nobody can sue; privacy-safe personalization; win-win subscriptions.
20. All platforms; new domain, Firebase project and repo per product; ready to plug in the paid domain, cloud and payment gateway; no fake data.
21. Review at every screen size (320 to 1920), not only 390 px. Settings in a small settings window; many tabs go in a simple side menu; RTL and LTR both correct.
22. Each product has its own icon, favicon and a logo in the navigation bar.
23. SIR Jobs: no yellow buttons, fix broken cards and buttons, make it simpler.
24. SIR Negm Furniture: improve its plans (not frozen), then hand it to the friend. No build work until he says so.

## Plans and handover
