Done. Here's the honest state of the work.

**What I actually did**
- **Avatar zoom slider**: no longer painted as a grey pill. The input now sits in a 44px row with a scoped `avatar-zoom-track` class: 6px rounded track, 20px solid accent thumb, no native white ring, no `accent-color`.
- **Crop/rotate**: new `rotateState` remaps pan across quarter-turns (rotation no longer jumps or shows empty edges). Pinch-to-zoom and two-finger pan added, all sharing one state with the slider and zoom buttons. The crop sheet is now a real fixed overlay modal above the tab bar (backdrop/X/Escape close, safe-area padding).
- **Keyboard**: global `overflow:hidden` pin is now scoped to chat screens only; non-chat screens keep scrolling and gain `--kb` bottom room. New `useKeyboardFocusReveal` scrolls the focused field into view. Mounted app-wide.
- **Switch (white circle)**: removed the duplicate dead white-knob rule; inline drag styles are now cleared on lost-pointer-capture and on unmount, so a gesture can never strand a scaled knob outside the track.
- **Buttons**: every crop-sheet button is ≥44px, has `active:scale`, a focus ring, `whitespace-nowrap`, and RTL-safe layout.

**Evidence**: tsc clean, eslint clean, 9 node tests pass, `npm run build` succeeds, bot-gateway tests 14/14. Screenshots (320/390px) in `AHome/.sir/evidence/r71-20261113/`. Committed straight to AHome main (`212af85`) and pushed; `_SIR` ledger/checkpoint updated (`df2ded5`). The r64 bot-kit files were committed too (verified there). CI shows 4-second zero-step failures — that is the Actions quota flag, not the code.

**Not done / needs you**: nothing has been seen on your phone. Your phone was locked and the install was blocked (`INSTALL_FAILED_USER_RESTRICTED`), so your installed APK predates all of this — the toggle overflow and button issues you photographed could not be confirmed fixed on-device. The reply file `D:/Projects/_SIR/ops/backup-manager/reply-1794529170535-1.txt` states exactly that in Arabic and asks you to unlock the phone so the new build can be installed and verified. I deliberately did not mark the autopilot task r71 done; that gate should close after the phone check. The GitHub `_SIR` push went through after one transient failure; AHome pushes verified via `ls-remote`.

Also worth knowing: the keyboard-open screenshot cannot emulate a real IME on a desktop browser, so the final "bio above keyboard" moment still needs your phone to confirm.
